From 7116d655a353cd100c8f8205dc80e458c7e810e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:50:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: external GS snapshot only on demand

Every VBlankStart called PS2ExternalGS::snapshot(), and the PCSX2 adapter's
snapshot flushes the GS and reads the display rect back (a GPU-to-CPU sync per
vsync on Vulkan), although only the frame dump and script capture steps use
the frame. The external GS presents into its own window and never needs it.

- gs_external.h: ps2SetExternalGSFrameDemand(fn) / ps2ExternalGSFrameWanted(tick).
  The scheduler calls snapshot() only when the demand function wants that tick;
  null (the default) = no snapshot. The snapshot now runs after the script step,
  so a capture step that begins at a tick gets that tick's frame.
- GS::publishExternalFrame(frame, tick) and latchedHostPresentationTick(): the
  published frame carries the vsync it was taken at.
- Ps2InputScript::captureWanted() (demand while a capture step needs frames);
  takeCapture refuses frames older than the capture step's first tick.
- UploadFrame with an external GS: no latch, copy or texture upload unless a
  frame consumer exists (PS2X_FRAME_DUMP_DIR); consumers get the frame's own tick.
- initialize: script with capture steps -> demand = captureWanted; plain
  PS2X_FRAME_DUMP_DIR -> every frame.

Tests: no demand, 6 vsyncs -> 0 snapshots; demand for ticks 2 and 4 -> exactly
those snapshots, latched frame tick 4; script capture demand and stale-frame
refusal.
